      "writtenOn": "2025-04-04T15:01:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right, there might be scenarios where only renderView is needed. But for chrome use cases, we almost can always provide both. And most of the time, both views are the same (because Chrome\u0027s shared images like D3D, IOSurface backing doesn\u0027t have mipmaps). So probably we can make this simpler by providing only one `view` parameter? This view will be used as both render and sample view in the `DawnTexture`.",
